<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Optional, off by default: the hazard vacuum setting gives VFEP's hazard warcasket the vacuum
    resistance of VFEP's spacer (10th generation) sets, a step above its own tier, to set the two
    7th-gen environment sets further apart under Odyssey. The Hazard is the all-rounder (fire,
    heat, cold, toxins, psychic) and the Toxin the tox gas specialist; without this, neither
    resists vacuum, as no 7th-gen set does. PatchOperationHazardVacuum skips the whole patch
    while the setting is off or Odyssey is inactive.

    Values per piece, as the spacer sets carry them:
    - VFEP alone: armor 0.2, shoulders 0.1, helmet 0.7, a 1.0 set.
    - Vanilla Gravship Expanded (chapter 1): its ArmorVacuumResistancePatch.xml lowers the
      spacer armors to 0.22 and helmets to 0.65 by defName, shoulders left at 0.1, so no suit
      reaches 1.0 without an oxygen source; the hazard takes those, matched by package id.
      An oxygen pack (VGE chapter 2, active from a base 0.12) then lifts it to 1.0 as it does
      the spacer sets.
    VGE's patch never names the hazard defs, so the two do not depend on load order. Any
    VacuumResistance already on the hazard (a future VFEP value, or a mod loaded before this
    one) is removed first, so the values below replace it rather than duplicate the stat.

    Save Our Ship 2: VFEP's own SOS2Patch.xml gives the hazard armor and helmet the EVA tag and
    Insulation_Cold 100. SOS2's vacuum survival runs on its own decompression and hypoxia
    stats, not VacuumResistance, and this patch touches neither those nor the EVA tag.
  -->
  <Operation Class="ToxinWarcasket.PatchOperationHazardVacuum">
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard" or defName = "VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Hazard" or defName = "VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Hazard"]/equippedStatOffsets/VacuumResistance</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Hazard"]/equippedStatOffsets</xpath>
          <value>
            <VacuumResistance>0.1</VacuumResistance>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="ToxinWarcasket.PatchOperationModActive">
          <packageIds>
            <li>vanillaexpanded.gravship</li>
          </packageIds>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard"]/equippedStatOffsets</xpath>
                <value>
                  <VacuumResistance>0.22</VacuumResistance>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Hazard"]/equippedStatOffsets</xpath>
                <value>
                  <VacuumResistance>0.65</VacuumResistance>
                </value>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </match>
          <nomatch Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "VFEP_Warcasket_Hazard"]/equippedStatOffsets</xpath>
                <value>
                  <VacuumResistance>0.2</VacuumResistance>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Hazard"]/equippedStatOffsets</xpath>
                <value>
                  <VacuumResistance>0.7</VacuumResistance>
                </value>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </nomatch>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
